 ## Background
-Independent Block Encoding is a fundamental component of deferred filtering architectures for compressed volumes [Parent]. It is often applied within a multiresolution framework, encoding blocks at various resolution levels obtained by digital filtering and subsampling [S2]. The approach is inspired by image compression standards like JPEG (using DCT) and has been adapted for 3D volumes using DFT, DCT, and Wavelets [S1]. Key references include Chiueh et al. for DFT-based encoding [CYH*97], YL95 for DCT-based encoding, and Lippert et al. for wavelet-based encoding [LGK97]. The method addresses the limitations of global transforms by enabling on-the-fly decoding on GPUs, where blocks are decomposed into parallel stripes [Parent].
